<http://data.silknow.org/object/c3ee61b8-11f1-3f74-97f9-8e09c7976333/observation/3>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "MAN’S ROBE\nGoat hair (pashmina), Woven and embroidered\nKashmir\nc. 1855\n05597 (IS)\n\nKashmiri embroidery was originally done on shawls in imitation of woven patterns, but from about 1830 new figurative designs were developed. This robe (choga) is decorated with turbaned and bearded Sikh figures combined with Iranian winged beings (peris) and dragons. Europeans are also shown, sitting in western-style chairs.\nThis robe may have come from the wardrobe store of the Maharaja of Jammu and Kashmir. [27/9/2013]"@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/c3ee61b8-11f1-3f74-97f9-8e09c7976333> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/c3ee61b8-11f1-3f74-97f9-8e09c7976333/category/1>
